      "message": "Nit/optional: There is a slightly simpler way to manage `initial_col`. However, it requires updating `initial_col` at the end of the outer for loop. Since the loop body is very long, this may make the code harder to understand:\n\n```\n  int initial_col \u003d 0;\n  for (int r \u003d 0; r + kBlockHeight \u003c\u003d height; r +\u003d kBlockHeight) {\n    for (int c \u003d initial_col; c + kBlockWidth \u003c\u003d width;\n         c +\u003d kBlockWidth * multiplier) {\n       ...\n    }\n#ifdef OUTPUT_SCR_DET_MODE2_STATS\n    fprintf(stats_file, \"\\n\");\n#endif\n    // Alternate skipping in a \"checkerboard\" pattern in fast detection mode\n    if (fast_detection_mode) {\n      initial_col \u003d kBlockWidth - initial_col;\n    }\n  }\n```",
