      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit: \"Return\" is ambiguous now that the function has a return value. We can say \"Set *num_colors to the number of colors in src.\"\n\nDocument what the boolean return value means. The following is what I gathered by reading the implementation:\n\n\u003e If the function returns true, `*num_colors` is accurate (and is `\u003c\u003d num_colors_threshold`). If the function returns false, `*num_colors` may be smaller than the actual value (and is `\u003e num_colors_threshold`).\n\nSo the return value is equal to `*num_colors \u003c\u003d num_colors_threshold`. The function doesn\u0027t really need to return it; the caller can calculate that easily.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 282,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 282,
